            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to General Wall, the United States (petitioner) argues that Congress, in Article\u202f43, intended the phrase \u201coffense punishable by death\u201d to refer to the punishments already set out in the UCMJ, such as the death penalty for rape in Article\u202f120."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Stephen I. Vladeck",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3bebd0653690-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Stephen I. Vladeck, Article\u202f55 reflects Congress's specific judgment that service members should receive the same protection against cruel and unusual punishment that civilians enjoy under the Eighth Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Vladeck",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3bebd0653690-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 52,
              "start": 52
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Vladeck, Article\u202f55, as it has been uniformly interpreted for 70\u202fyears, applies the Coker rule to courts\u2011martial."
      }
    ],
