              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to General Wall, the case concerns whether the statute of limitations applies to rape offenses punishable by death under Article\u202f43 of the Uniform Code of Military Justice (UCMJ)."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "General Wall",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Wall, congress intended Article\u202f43\u2019s reference to \u201coffense punishable by death\u201d to mean offenses for which the UCMJ already provides a death penalty, such as rape under Article\u202f120."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "General Wall",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Wall, the limitations provision should be read in context with the penalty provision, not as a separate, standalone rule."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "General Wall",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to General Wall, the usual reading of limitations provisions does not apply here; extensive textual, contextual, and historical evidence shows Congress was not limiting the death\u2011penalty provision."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Vladeck",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0002-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Vladeck, according to Stephen I. Vladeck, Article\u202f55, as uniformly interpreted for 70\u202fyears, applies the Coker rule to courts\u2011martial."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Vladeck",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0002-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Vladeck, even if the text were read to add the words the government proposes, Article\u202f55 still leads to the same result because it applies the Coker rule to courts\u2011martial."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Vladeck",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 48,
                "start": 48
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Vladeck, the respondents argue that \u201coffense punishable by death\u201d does not create a separate offense for juveniles or diminished\u2011capacity offenders; it is merely a charge based on capacity."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondents",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3bebd06536902936b95d03e16f95fe8c7c9aafb0aad869347b1110bb087845db",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3bebd0653690-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 64,
                "start": 64
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondents, the respondents\u2019 plain\u2011meaning argument did not address the parallel language between Articles\u202f43 and\u202f120 or the express language of Article\u202f18 regarding death authorization."
        }
      ],
